Nefer for gcsim, from an unmerged gcsim pull request, moved onto gcsim v2.50.0 (+ linnea.patch),
plus fixes for the problems gcsim's tests and review found.

Source: https://github.com/genshinsim/gcsim/pull/3045 ("Nefer try 2") by dersario, commits d833248
        and 4932d0e (2026-09-20), based on an older gcsim (d6be803); replayed onto v2.50.0 with
        linnea.patch applied, without conflicts. Apply after linnea.patch (patches apply in name order).
Not reviewed or accepted by gcsim's maintainers: results are experimental.

Left out: the website files (ui/).

Verdant Dew: the pull request adds a general "Verdant Dew rate" hook to gcsim's player code. Only
Nefer (her ascension passive and C4) uses it; without her, Dew generation is unchanged (checked with
a Lunar-Bloom team: identical results with and without this patch).

Fixes added by this project:
  - Marked "incomplete" in gcsim (as linnea.patch does for Linnea), so every result with her shows
    gcsim's "may not match the game exactly yet" warning.
  - Plunge removed: it dealt damage but had no frames, so gcsim's ability test crashed, and its
    timings were never counted. Plunging gives gcsim's usual "not implemented" error.
  - Normal attack 4: the animation (51) was shorter than its measured walk cancel (63); now 63.
  - Burst energy: ConsumeEnergy(60) drained energy 60 frames late (the argument is a delay, not an
    amount). Her drain frame isn't counted; 4 frames, the delay gcsim uses most often.
  - Burst damage bonus from Veil stacks: it lasted 90 frames and ended before both hits (104, 149),
    so it never applied. It now lasts until the second hit (150 frames), as gcsim's review asked.
  - Slither (held charged attack) no longer walks her towards the enemy (no other gcsim character
    moves the player; the review asked for it). Seeds of Deceit appear around the enemy, inside her
    6 m pickup radius.

Known open points (not changed here): most of her kit hasn't been reviewed by gcsim yet; the Seeds
of Deceit pickup radius (6 m) is the author's assumption; untested fixes proposed in review
(Phantasm second hit after a cancel, C6 end hit) aren't included.

This file is applied by scripts/build-gcsim.sh. When gcsim includes Nefer itself, the build skips
it and says so; then delete this file.

